# Design Conventions

## Uniformity (always)

- Keep chrome consistent across related surfaces: same control placement, grouping, sizing, and hover behavior.
- Icon-only buttons **must** have a hover tooltip (use `Tooltip` + `TooltipTrigger` + `TooltipContent`) with a short label matching `aria-label`.
- Group related toolbar actions in one bordered bar (`rounded-lg border bg-background/90 p-1 shadow-sm backdrop-blur`) instead of scattering separate controls.
- Reuse the same pattern when a control appears in more than one mode (e.g. map and list): same corner, same container styles, same tooltip wording.
- Prefer existing shared components (`ViewModeToggle`, `Heading`, `FormSidebar`, `DataTable`, `Modal` / `ConfirmDialog`, `components/ui/*`) over one-off variants.
- Do not introduce a new visual language for a single page when a sibling page already solved the same UI problem.

## Breadcrumb bar actions

Primary page actions for list/index screens live in the breadcrumb header bar (right side), not in a page `Heading` row.

- Set them with Inertia `setLayoutProps({ headerActions })` inside a `useEffect` (never during render). Call `resetLayoutProps()` on unmount.
- Primary “create / new” actions use a leading `Plus` icon at `size-4` before the label (e.g. `New user`, `New role`).
- When the page supports row selection for bulk delete, show a destructive action in the same header group when one or more rows are selected (e.g. `Delete 5 users`), with a leading `Trash2` icon at `size-4`.
- Selection-dependent header actions must **fade** in and out (`transition-opacity duration-200`): keep mounted while fading out, then unmount after ~200ms; keep the last count label during the exit fade.
- Put header action buttons in one `flex items-center gap-2` group.

## Page headers

- A page header (title + subtext) is used **only** when the page has action button(s) in its **in-page** header row (not the breadcrumb bar).
- If a page has in-page header actions: render a title and a short subtext on the left, with the action button(s) on the right (`flex items-start justify-between`). Use the `Heading` component for the title + description.
- Keep the header close to the content: give the header row `mb-4` and pass `className="mb-0"` to `Heading` so its default `mb-8` doesn't stack with the row margin.
- If a page has **no** in-page header actions (e.g. the dashboard, or list pages that only use breadcrumb `headerActions`): render **no** page header at all — the breadcrumb bar provides context. Do not add a lone title or an intro/subtitle paragraph.
- Never add a standalone description paragraph without a title.

## Buttons

- Primary “create / new” actions use a leading `Plus` icon at `size-4` before the label (e.g. `New role`, `New System`, `New table`).
- Destructive bulk actions use `variant="destructive"` with a leading `Trash2` icon at `size-4`.
- Match sibling pages: same icon size, placement, and casing pattern for equivalent actions.
- Icon-only buttons still require a hover tooltip (see Uniformity above).

## Data tables

Use the shared `DataTable` (`@/components/data-table`) for list indexes.

- Search (default on): pass `searchPlaceholder`; mark searchable fields with `searchValue` on columns.
- Sort: set `sortable` + `sortValue` on columns; header toggles ascending / descending.
- Pagination: client-side by default (`pageSize`, default `10`) with Previous / Next and result range.
- Selection (when needed): enable `selection` so the checkbox column is **first**.
- Row delete (when needed): pass `onDelete`. The delete column has a **blank header**, a centered `Trash2` icon button (`text-destructive`, `hover:bg-destructive/10`), tooltip/`aria-label` **Delete**, and `stopPropagation` so it does not fire `onRowClick`.
- Row publish (when needed): pass `onPublish` / `canPublish`. Unpublished rows use an `Upload` icon with tooltip/`aria-label` **Publish**. Published rows with pending `unpub_shape` changes use `isSync` so the action shows a `RefreshCw` icon with tooltip/`aria-label` **Sync**. Show for unpublished tables and for published tables with pending changes.
- Prefer `onRowClick` to open edit in a `FormSidebar` rather than a separate edit icon column.
- Do **not** use `window.confirm` / `alert` for delete — use `ConfirmDialog`.

## Modals & confirmations

Use `Modal` / `ConfirmDialog` from `@/components/modal`. Do **not** use browser `confirm()` or `alert()`. Prefer these over raw `Dialog` for app-facing prompts.

### Visual layout (required)

Match the centered status-dialog pattern:

1. **Icon** (optional on `Modal`, default on `ConfirmDialog`) — `size-12` circular badge above the title; icon glyph at `size-6`.
   - `tone` / `variant`: `default` → `bg-primary/15 text-primary`; `success` → `bg-emerald-500/15 text-emerald-500` + `Check`; `destructive` → `bg-destructive/15 text-destructive` + `TriangleAlert`.
2. **Title** — centered, `text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight`.
3. **Description** — centered, `text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground`.
4. **Actions** — one row, equal width: Cancel `variant="outline" size="lg" className="flex-1"`, confirm `size="lg" className="flex-1"` (`default` or `destructive`). Footer uses `flex-row gap-3`.
5. **Chrome** — `rounded-xl p-8 sm:max-w-md gap-6`; `showCloseButton` defaults to **false** (no X). Dismiss via Cancel, overlay click, or Escape.

### Behavior

- Destructive confirms: `ConfirmDialog` with `variant="destructive"`, clear title + description, confirm label like `Delete` / `Deactivate`.
- Success-style confirms: `variant="success"` (check icon).
- Keep `open` separate from the pending payload so content stays stable during close; clear payload after ~200ms.
- Cancel uses `DialogClose` (or controlled `onOpenChange(false)`) so the overlay unmounts cleanly.
- Block dismiss while `processing` is true.

## Form sidebars

- Use `FormSidebar` (`@/components/form-sidebar`) for create/edit panels: right sheet, `sm:max-w-2xl`, children own body/footer so borders can span full width.
- Open create from breadcrumb `headerActions`; open edit from `DataTable` `onRowClick`.

## Icon + name editors (sheets / side panels)

When an entity has a changeable icon and a name field (roles, tables, map edit panels):

- Place the icon and name on one row: `flex items-end gap-3`.
- Icon control: clickable `size-12` button (`rounded-xl border bg-muted/40`), icon at `size-7`, with hover border/background and a **Change icon** tooltip/`aria-label`. Do **not** use a separate “Change icon” text link.
- Name field: `flex-1` beside the icon (label + input stacked). Put the name field **first in the DOM** and use `order-1` / `order-2` so sheet auto-focus prefers the input. For the Change icon control, use a **hover-only** controlled tooltip (`open` driven by `onPointerEnter` / `onPointerLeave`) so sheet focus does not show the popover on open.
- Icon picker opens below that row: full-width responsive grid (`grid-cols-6 sm:grid-cols-8 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-2`) with compact `h-10` option buttons (active: `border-primary bg-primary/10 text-primary`).
- Keep the same pattern across list sheets and map floating panels; only the picker placement may differ (inline vs adjacent panel) when space requires it.

## Layout & structure

- Pages use `AppLayout` (via the global resolver) with a `PageName.layout = { breadcrumbs: [...] }` static.
- Full-screen experiences (e.g. the editor) opt out of `AppLayout` in `app.tsx` and provide their own chrome.
- Wrap page content in `px-4 py-6` (or a centered `max-w-*` for forms).

## Components & styling

- Reuse the existing `components/ui/*` (shadcn/radix) kit before writing new components.
- Use theme tokens (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border`, `bg-primary/10`, `text-destructive`) — never hardcoded colors, so dark mode works.
- Group related content in bordered sections/`Card`s; keep vertical rhythm with `space-y-*` and `gap-*`.
- Use `lucide-react` icons at `size-4`/`size-5`; verify the icon name exists before importing.

## Validation

- Never rely on browser HTML5 validation popups (`required`, `pattern`, native “Please fill out this field.” tooltips).
- Always use `noValidate` on app forms that submit to Laravel, and show errors with `InputError` from server (or matching client) validation messages.
- Prefer Laravel Form Request validation as the source of truth; inline errors under each field.
- **Clear on edit:** when a field shows a validation error (e.g. required), clear that field’s error as soon as the user starts editing it — typing, changing a select/toggle, or otherwise updating the control. Use Inertia `clearErrors('field')` (or the local equivalent). Do this for **every** form field that can display an `InputError`, not only required checks. Do not wait for the next submit to hide the message.

## Tags / System badges

Tags are always rendered as **pill badges** via `TagBadge` (`@/components/tag-badge`) — never plain text or a bare `Badge` without an icon.

- In the UI, label this column/field **System** (DB column remains `tag`).
- Shape: `rounded-full`, icon (`size-3.5`) + label, `gap-1.5`, `px-2.5 py-0.5`, `text-xs font-medium`.
- Light mode: soft tinted background (`bg-{color}-500/15`) + matching text.
- Dark mode: dark fill (`dark:bg-background`) + thin colored border + matching text.
- **Ciian** tag: icon + system name from `ciian_config`; tint uses `ciian_config.color` (editable).
- **No System** (`tag === 'no_system'`): muted badge + **CircleDashed** icon; UI label **No System** (legacy; not used for new creates).
- **System tables** (`ciian_sys_tbl`): badge label is the system name; icon comes from the parent `System.icon` (via `getSystemIcon`).
- **Internal tables** (`ciian_int_tbl`): badge label is `tag`; icon comes from the row’s `icon` column (default `Sparkles` for Ciian).
- On create: System is selectable from **Ciian** + created systems (`ciian_sys`). On edit: System is **locked** (read-only badge).
- **Ciian** (create or seeded) → `ciian_int_tbl`. **Created systems** → `ciian_sys_tbl`. **No System** is legacy only (not offered on create).
- Systems index **Tag** column shows `TagBadge` (icon + name) for each row.
- New table form uses a **column builder** (not raw JSON). Auto Increment `id` is always present and locked.

## Navigation

- Use Inertia `<Link>` (not `<a>`) for internal navigation.
